    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm managing a rental property in phoenix and the tenant is complaining that the ac is running constantly but one of the bedrooms stays really hot. what are some common reasons why one room would just stay warm like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Common causes for a single room running hot include an incorrect thermostat placement, blocked vents, or insufficient insulation in that specific zone. You should check if a thermostat thermostat is directly under the window or near a heat source, and verify that air vents are not covered by furniture or storage items. Additionally, solar heat gain could be trapped in that bedroom if large windows or improper shading are present, while duct leaks can also prevent cool air from reaching that specific area. Consulting a licensed HVAC technician to perform a leak test or seal around radiators is recommended to rule out hidden mechanical failures.",
