    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the vents seem fine and nothing is blocking them. i checked the insulation too and looks okay. could there be something more \"hidden\" going on inside the walls or the ductwork that we cant see just by looking at it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, hidden duct leaks or incorrect air return placement inside the walls can easily starve a room of cool air without any visible blockage. HVAC systems also have a default strategy that prioritizes energy efficiency over uniform temperature, sometimes sending cold air elsewhere first or recirculating hot air within the specific bedroom zone. It is highly recommended to hire a specialized duct pros or HVAC contractor to inspect the hidden run to identify these invisible airflow obstructions or proper duct sealing.",
